\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 \column At the Opening Menu, the \ul Left\ulnone  button \b selects\b0  the file or subdirectory the cursor is pointing to, or, if you are not pointing to a file or subdirectory, it then pulls down the \b File menu\b0 .  If a menu is currently pulled down, then the left button selects whatever menu choice you point to.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 The \ul Right\ulnone  button safely \b cancels\b0 .  If your cursor is in the file directory, it jumps the cursor back up to the pulldown menu bar.  If a menu has been pulled down, the right button closes the pulldown menu without making a selection.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 The middle button and the mouse chords (simultaneous presses of multiple buttons) are disabled at the Opening Menu.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
