\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 The \ul Left\ulnone  button logs the subdirectory specified by name in the dialog box, if the cursor is there, or logs the subdirectory highlighted in the directory listing.  Tip:  A quick way to navigate your current disk is to point-and-shoot at the \b ..\b0  directory entry to move up to the parent of the current subdirectory, then point-and- shoot again at the subdirectory you want.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 The \ul Middle\ulnone  button pops up a point-and-shoot listing of drive letters.  The default order is:}\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
