\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 \column The \ul Left\ulnone  button brings down the File \b pulldown menu\b0  if you are editing, or makes a selection from a pulldown menu if you are already in a menu.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 The \ul Middle\ulnone  button \b marks the sentence\b0  containing the cursor as a block.  Pressing the middle button again marks the next sentence in the document.  MICKEE defines a sentence by the method recommended in most style guides for manuscript format, requiring two spaces after the terminal punctuation.  This way, sentences ending with punctuation other than periods will be marked correctly and abbreviations such as "Dr." will not confuse MICKEE about where a sentence ends.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 The \ul Right\ulnone  button \b marks the paragraph\b0  containing the cursor as a block.  Pressing the right button again marks the next paragraph in the document.  MICKEE defines a paragraph as text beginning and ending with a single hard carriage return, so you can also use this feature to mark isolated lines, such as titles.  Paragraphs can be indented or not as you please.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 Pressing the \ul Left and Middle\ulnone  buttons simultaneously will set WordStar's \b BEGIN block marker\b0 , <B>, just as if you had issued ^KB.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 Pressing the \ul Middle and Right\ulnone  buttons simultaneously will set WordStar's \b END block marker\b0 , <K>, just as if you had issued ^KK.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 Pressing the \ul Left and Right\ulnone  buttons simultaneously will \b move\b0  the currently marked block, reformatting the text both at the source and destination locations, and then hide the block.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 Pressing \ul All Three\ulnone  buttons simultaneously will \b hide\b0  the currently marked block, if it is visible, or reveal the currently marked block, if it is hidden, just as if you had issued ^KH.  }\sect
