\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 In the \b Spelling\b0  dialog box, these choices will let you select WordStar's suggested corrections by number, or issue the More, Bypass, Add, Enter Correction, Global replace, Ignore, or Exclude commands.   }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 In the \b Size-Window\b0  dialog box, these choices will let you select a full screen for each document, or one-half screen in normal 25-line mode, 43-line EGA mode, or 50- line VGA mode.  }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 }\par
\pard\plain\kerning1\ql\li0\ri0\fi-144\sl-240\slmult0\tx720{\f0\fs24 In the \b Go-to-Page\b0  dialog box, you will have the option of pointing and shooting at specific page numbers from 1 to 18, or selecting the next (N) or previous (P) page.  }\par
